title: REMS
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''REMS:'' Risk Evaluation and Mitigation Strategy—an FDA-required program ensuring benefits outweigh serious medication risks.
* ''Lenalidomide rationale:'' Prevent embryo-fetal exposure; severe birth defects or fetal death may occur.
* ''Access:'' Certified prescribers/pharmacies; enrolled, counseled patients with signed agreements.
* ''Before prescribing:'' Verify required pregnancy tests, pregnancy-prevention compliance, and applicable patient/prescriber surveys.
** Obtain authorization; include authorization number and patient risk category on every prescription.
* ''Dispensing:'' Certified pharmacy supplies ≤28 days; no automatic refills.

Sources: [[FDA REMS FAQ|https://www.fda.gov/drugs/risk-evaluation-and-mitigation-strategies-rems/frequently-asked-questions-faqs-about-rems]]; [[Lenalidomide REMS|https://www.lenalidomiderems.com/prescriber-resources/index.html]]; [[US label §5.1–5.2|https://packageinserts.bms.com/pi/pi_revlimid.pdf]].
